{"type":"message","id":"5de6a1ef","parentId":"edb1b1b5","timestamp":"2026-03-19T14:18:50.226Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"320\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"495506013\",\n  \"sender\": \"Matteo Cicalese\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Thu 2026-03-19 14:17 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Matteo Cicalese (495506013)\",\n  \"id\": \"495506013\",\n  \"name\": \"Matteo Cicalese\",\n  \"username\": \"CicaMatt\"\n}\n```\n\nfor now the actual image is not uploaded through the endpoint, even tho in returns a path and it does not seem to give errors. the following is the actual code of the endpoint that is reached. try to adapt the request so that you satisfy the requirements of this implementation\n\nimplementation of the endpoint:\n\"@router.post(\"/input/upload\")\nasync def upload(\n file: UploadFile,\n storage_ref: str,\n local_file_path: str,\n user_id: str,\n # payload: str = Form(...),\n s3_client: BaseClient = Depends(s3_client),\n):\n \"\"\"\n It uploads the file to s3 bucket INPUT_STORAGE and run the first node.\n \"\"\"\n # _payload = Payload[input.UploadDataReaderInput].parse_raw(payload)\n local_file_path = (\n os.path.join(\n local_file_path,\n datetime.now().strftime(\"%m-%d-%Y_%H.%M.%S\")\n + \"_\"\n + generate_random_string(20),\n )\n + \"/\"\n )\n try:\n # workflow_name = _payload.metadata.workflow_name\n # if _payload.data.filename is None:\n # _payload.data.filename = f\"input/{workflow_name}/{file.filename}\"\n\n # s3_client, bucket = storageRefResolver(_payload.data.storage_ref)\n log.debug(\"file_name {}\".format(file.filename))\n log.debug(\"file_size {}\".format(file.file.fileno()))\n log.debug(\"local_file_path {}\".format(local_file_path))\n found = MINIO_CLIENT.bucket_exists(storage_ref)\n\n if not found:\n MINIO_CLIENT.make_bucket(storage_ref)\n\n if file.filename.find(\"/\") != -1:\n log.debug(\"MINIO_CLIENT {}\".format(file.filename))\n local_file_path = \"\"\n # MINIO_CLIENT.fput_object(\n # storage_ref,\n # file.filename,\n # file.file.fileno(),\n # )\n object = MINIO_CLIENT.get_object(storage_ref, file.filename)\n else:\n MINIO_CLIENT.fput_object(\n storage_ref,\n os.path.join(local_file_path, file.filename),\n file.file.fileno(),\n )\n object = MINIO_CLIENT.get_object(\n storage_ref, os.path.join(local_file_path, file.filename)\n )\n if file.filename.endswith(\".csv\"): # the file is a .csv\n file_encoding = chardet.detect(\n BytesIO(object.data).getvalue()\n ) # detected file encoding\n sample_data = BytesIO(object.data).read(1024)\n dialect = csv.Sniffer().sniff(\n sample_data.decode(file_encoding[\"encoding\"])\n ) # detected delimiter\n df = pd.read_csv(\n BytesIO(object.data),\n sep=dialect.delimiter,\n encoding=file_encoding[\"encoding\"],\n )\n column_names = df.columns.values.tolist()\n elif file.filename.endswith(\".xls\") or file.filename.endswith(\n \".xlsx\"\n ): # the file is a .xls/.xlsx\n df = pd.ExcelFile(BytesIO(object.data))\n sheet_names = df.sheet_names\n column_names = dict()\n for sheet in sheet_names:\n columns = df.parse(sheet).columns\n column_names[sheet] = list(columns)\n else:\n column_names = None\n\n return [\n {\n \"path\": local_file_path,\n \"filename\": file.filename,\n \"column_names\": column_names,\n }\n ] # input.UploadDataReader().run()#_payload\n\n except Exception as e:\n #print(e)\n #log.error(e)\n #log.exception(e)\n return {\"Error\": e}\""}],"timestamp":1773929930221}}
