{"type":"message","id":"b9d4db13","parentId":"18db66bc","timestamp":"2026-03-19T14:19:48.124Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_DL6Z3yuHHk6b1B5N3eDGtU5r|fc_03fe980ae38bea510169bc0603f15481919e56218b985ac972","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload&user_id=495506013\n['curl', '-sS', '-X', 'POST', 'http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload&user_id=495506013', '-H', 'accept: application/json', '-F', 'file=@/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_1---f8051025-be40-4c1a-bba9-e4f1806083a6.jpg;type=image/jpeg']"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":53,"aggregated":"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload&user_id=495506013\n['curl', '-sS', '-X', 'POST', 'http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload&user_id=495506013', '-H', 'accept: application/json', '-F', 'file=@/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_1---f8051025-be40-4c1a-bba9-e4f1806083a6.jpg;type=image/jpeg']","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773929988119}}
{"type":"message","id":"963491da","parentId":"b9d4db13","timestamp":"2026-03-19T14:19:57.332Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The script is updated. It now uploads using a native curl multipart form request with `-F file=@...;type=...`, which is a much closer match to what that FastAPI endpoint expects.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_03fe980ae38bea510169bc060643e881919056e0975284e715\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] I adapted the upload step to match the endpoint implementation more closely.\n\nWhat changed:\n- The skill script now sends the upload via a native curl-style multipart request\n- It uses:\n  - query params: `storage_ref`, `local_file_path`, `user_id`\n  - multipart field: `file`\n  - file forwarding format equivalent to:\n    `-F 'file=@...;type=image/jpeg'`\n\nWhy this should help:\n- That endpoint is explicitly expecting `file: UploadFile` from multipart form data\n- My previous version manually constructed the multipart body\n- The new version lets curl generate the multipart payload the way FastAPI/Starlette usually expects\n\nThe request is now effectively shaped like:\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \\\n  'http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload&user_id=495506013' \\\n  -H 'accept: application/json' \\\n  -F 'file=@/path/to/image.jpg;type=image/jpeg'\n```\n\nWhat it means:\n- If the image still is not really ending up in storage, the issue is less likely to be the request format now\n- At that point, the problem is probably inside the endpoint/server side behavior around `MINIO_CLIENT.fput_object(...)`, `file.file.fileno()`, or how the uploaded temp file is being handled\n\nNext sensible step:\n- If you want, I can run one more live test with the updated uploader and report the exact returned path again, so we can confirm whether this new request shape changes the server behavior.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\