{"type":"message","id":"a07a5b82","parentId":"04ae8186","timestamp":"2026-03-19T14:22:44.880Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Ran it with the updated uploader.\n\n**Upload step**\n- Request URL used:\n  `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload&user_id=495506013`\n- Returned `path`:\n  `upload/2026-03-19_14.23.09_86DpQ7SLdRwShypYAq7a/`\n- Returned `filename`:\n  `file_1---36f964c8-5b24-4242-9f7f-92b06ec6119e.jpg`\n- Full uploaded image path:\n  `upload/2026-03-19_14.23.09_86DpQ7SLdRwShypYAq7a/file_1---36f964c8-5b24-4242-9f7f-92b06ec6119e.jpg`\n\n**Result**\n- The endpoint still accepts the upload and returns a fresh path.\n- The downstream pipeline still returns the same analysis output and same analyzer image URL as before.\n\nSo at this point:\n- the **request format is now aligned much more closely** with the endpoint contract\n- but the server behavior still suggests the file is either not actually being persisted/read correctly, or the later pipeline stage is not using the newly uploaded object\n\nMost likely server-side issue in that endpoint:\n- `MINIO_CLIENT.fput_object(..., file.file.fileno())` looks suspicious\n- `fput_object` normally expects a **file path string**, not a file descriptor integer\n- if that code really runs as shown, it could explain why you get a returned path without a real uploaded object\n\nIf you want, next I can help you patch the **endpoint implementation itself** to use the uploaded temp file correctly.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_03fe980ae38bea510169bc06ac564081919e692d83314b21f2\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":10494,"output":389,"cacheRead":46464,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":57347,"cost":{"input":0.026235,"output":0.005835,"cacheRead":0.011616,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.043686}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773930154290}}
